{
 "_comment": "Alert-unit coupling. `tie_*` groups alerted account-days by exact (day, score); unrelated transactions can share a score, so tie_groups is a LOWER bound on distinct transactions and tie_account_days_per_group is an UPPER bound on the over-counting factor. `*_ring_txn*` fields attribute an alert to the ring transaction whose own score EQUALS the account-day maximum -- the score source -- read from ring_transactions.parquet; an earlier version joined endpoints without that filter and therefore counted ring transactions that did not cause the alert. Ring transactions are the only ones whose identity and score these bundles record, so nothing here covers the full alerted set, and a transaction-level precision, recall or ceiling is NOT derivable from these fields. Earlier attempts at both are retracted.",
 "budgets": [
  50,
  200,
  1000
 ],
